WEBVTT

00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:31.130
<i>This is my big battle against Ono.</i>

00:00:35.900 --> 00:00:38.400
<i>SAMURAI SHODOWN III: BLADES OF BLOOD</i>

00:00:38.470 --> 00:00:39.800
<i>Samurai Shodown III.</i>

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:41.870
<i>I'm not confident enough yet.</i>

00:00:45.970 --> 00:00:47.010
<i>Street Fighter Alpha 2.</i>

00:00:48.710 --> 00:00:50.780
<i>I'm still not ready
for a one-on-one with this.</i>

00:00:52.280 --> 00:00:54.680
<i>I need a game I know I can defeat Ono at.</i>

00:00:56.320 --> 00:00:57.620
<i>You there!</i>

00:00:58.550 --> 00:01:01.090
<i>Are you truly so
hell-bent on being the victor?</i>

00:01:01.160 --> 00:01:02.960
HEAVEN

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:13.000
<i>Pitiful! Is that all the desire
you can muster?</i>

00:01:13.670 --> 00:01:14.740
I...

00:01:15.670 --> 00:01:17.140
want to win at any cost!

00:01:18.570 --> 00:01:20.380
No matter the means!

00:01:20.440 --> 00:01:22.610
<i>Then allow me to help you.</i>

00:01:23.180 --> 00:01:24.380
<i>I am...</i>

00:01:25.150 --> 00:01:27.480
<i>the master of the fist!</i>

00:01:29.220 --> 00:01:32.320
<i>Use your Shakunetsu Hadoken of love</i>

00:01:32.890 --> 00:01:37.030
<i>to burn your rival in romance to a crisp!</i>

00:01:43.430 --> 00:01:44.470
Ono.

00:01:46.400 --> 00:01:47.740
I can choose the game

00:01:48.470 --> 00:01:50.510
we fight each other in, right?

00:02:07.820 --> 00:02:11.790
ORIGINAL WORK BY RENSUKE OSHIKIRI

00:03:52.130 --> 00:03:53.260
<i>As a student,</i>

00:03:54.030 --> 00:03:56.400
<i>my life was dull and all I did was study.</i>

00:03:58.770 --> 00:04:01.840
<i>I became interested in Yaguchi
who always looked like he was having fun.</i>

00:04:02.770 --> 00:04:04.910
<i>I gradually became
more interested in games too.</i>

00:04:05.710 --> 00:04:08.880
<i>Before I knew it,
I was in love with Yaguchi.</i>

00:04:10.650 --> 00:04:13.350
<i>Thanks to him,
every day was fulfilling and fun.</i>

00:04:14.920 --> 00:04:18.320
<i>Yaguchi gave me something
I could become totally absorbed in.</i>

00:04:19.220 --> 00:04:21.890
<i>He taught me the joy of
becoming serious about something.</i>

00:04:22.720 --> 00:04:23.730
<i>I love him!</i>

00:04:25.460 --> 00:04:28.360
<i>I want to be with him forever.</i>

00:04:31.770 --> 00:04:32.770
But...

00:04:35.470 --> 00:04:37.170
<i>Until I defeat her,</i>

00:04:38.910 --> 00:04:40.240
<i>that will never happen.</i>

00:04:49.250 --> 00:04:51.190
<i>I'm so nervous, my hands are trembling.</i>

00:04:53.490 --> 00:04:55.190
<i>I know how to access Akuma.</i>

00:04:55.890 --> 00:04:57.290
<i>On the character selection screen...</i>

00:05:01.230 --> 00:05:02.360
<i>I screwed up!</i>

00:05:06.400 --> 00:05:08.840
<i>Wait! Ono is going for Akuma too!</i>

00:05:10.510 --> 00:05:12.070
<i>Hold on a second!</i>

00:05:12.540 --> 00:05:14.540
<i>My accidentally chosen Ryu</i>

00:05:14.610 --> 00:05:16.810
<i>doesn't stand a chance
against Ono's Akuma!</i>

00:05:17.880 --> 00:05:20.080
<i>She'll crush me!</i>

00:05:24.850 --> 00:05:25.850
<i>She screwed up?</i>

00:05:26.850 --> 00:05:30.330
<i>What a total disappointment
just before our big battle.</i>

00:05:32.260 --> 00:05:34.830
<i>It must mean Ono is nervous too.</i>

00:05:35.400 --> 00:05:39.970
Ono, let's say this one doesn't count,
and make the next one the real thing.

00:05:42.800 --> 00:05:44.170
<i>I need to calm down too.</i>

00:05:45.370 --> 00:05:47.510
<i>If Ono is going to
come after me with Akuma,</i>

00:05:48.010 --> 00:05:49.780
<i>she must know how equally matched we are.</i>

00:05:59.050 --> 00:06:00.290
<i>Doesn't Ono know?</i>

00:06:00.660 --> 00:06:02.620
<i>The odds in a Zangief
versus Akuma fight are</i>

00:06:03.160 --> 00:06:05.290
<i>nine-to-one in favor of Akuma.</i>

00:06:05.930 --> 00:06:07.400
<i>Some even give Akuma ten.</i>

00:06:07.830 --> 00:06:10.160
<i>That's how huge the gap is
between these two!</i>

00:06:12.030 --> 00:06:14.570
<i>Does this mean she has
a special attack up her sleeve?</i>

00:06:16.570 --> 00:06:19.570
<i>But she won't get any mercy from me!</i>

00:06:20.910 --> 00:06:24.180
<i>If I can win this fight, then I will!</i>

00:06:29.720 --> 00:06:31.150
<i>I don't care if it's unfair.</i>

00:06:31.890 --> 00:06:33.490
<i>I don't care if it's cowardly!</i>

00:06:34.760 --> 00:06:36.360
<i>I won't let him get near me!</i>

00:06:38.690 --> 00:06:39.930
<i>If victory</i>

00:06:40.730 --> 00:06:42.130
<i>gives me Yaguchi,</i>

00:06:43.730 --> 00:06:46.700
<i>then I will be as cruel as a demon!</i>

00:06:48.100 --> 00:06:49.170
<i>You may think it's craven.</i>

00:06:49.900 --> 00:06:52.310
<i>You may scorn me
for my greedy desire to win.</i>

00:06:52.610 --> 00:06:56.980
<i>But this is the only way
an ordinary person like me can defeat you.</i>

00:06:57.680 --> 00:07:01.320
<i>That's why I'll never stop
launching Zanku Hadoken!</i>

00:07:02.050 --> 00:07:03.820
<i>I'll keep launching them forever!</i>

00:07:04.650 --> 00:07:06.520
<i>I'll force her to stay on the defensive.</i>

00:07:06.590 --> 00:07:07.760
<i>I'll only let you defend!</i>

00:07:09.560 --> 00:07:12.460
<i>I don't care if I never get a proper hit.
I'll whittle you down!</i>

00:07:12.530 --> 00:07:14.800
<i>How will you overcome
your disadvantage, Ono?</i>

00:07:16.130 --> 00:07:17.570
<i>Show me your mettle!</i>

00:07:18.070 --> 00:07:22.200
<i>Show me just how strong
your feelings for Yaguchi are, Ono!</i>

00:07:26.110 --> 00:07:27.610
<i>That's the first win.</i>

00:07:28.740 --> 00:07:30.510
<i>I don't care how I win.</i>

00:07:31.050 --> 00:07:32.280
<i>Because...</i>

00:07:33.310 --> 00:07:35.280
<i>I've sold my soul to the devil!</i>

00:07:36.220 --> 00:07:37.890
<i>Wait for me, Yaguchi!</i>

00:07:38.190 --> 00:07:41.860
<i>I'll defeat Ono and come to be with you!</i>

00:07:45.190 --> 00:07:47.030
<i>She's in a totally helpless situation,</i>

00:07:47.530 --> 00:07:49.160
<i>so why is she still so serious?</i>

00:07:50.500 --> 00:07:54.640
<i>Is she still waiting for some chance
even though her situation is desperate?</i>

00:07:57.410 --> 00:07:59.110
<i>What does she see beyond</i>

00:07:59.910 --> 00:08:00.810
<i>my Zanku Hadoken?</i>

00:08:03.210 --> 00:08:04.650
<i>What are you waiting for?</i>

00:08:06.180 --> 00:08:09.080
<i>What kind of opening
are you waiting for, Ono?</i>

00:08:10.850 --> 00:08:12.490
<i>How can she be so patient?</i>

00:08:13.390 --> 00:08:15.820
<i>Finding a foolproof way to win
no matter the means.</i>

00:08:17.390 --> 00:08:19.160
<i>Isn't that how to win?</i>

00:08:21.830 --> 00:08:25.000
<i>I'm just playing the way that gives me
a 100-percent chance of winning.</i>

00:08:26.070 --> 00:08:27.340
<i>But...</i>

00:08:28.570 --> 00:08:30.440
<i>what is this feeling?</i>

00:08:32.270 --> 00:08:33.440
<i>Guilt?</i>

00:08:35.340 --> 00:08:40.210
<i>I don't care if this kind of attack is
contrary to my love of fighting games.</i>

00:08:42.520 --> 00:08:43.450
<i>Hidaka.</i>

00:08:44.720 --> 00:08:48.090
<i>I don't want to lose to anyone
who doesn't want to lose.</i>

00:08:49.660 --> 00:08:50.590
<i>Damn!</i>

00:08:53.660 --> 00:08:54.930
<i>Is it possible...</i>

00:08:55.960 --> 00:08:57.800
<i>that the chance you were waiting for...</i>

00:08:58.530 --> 00:09:00.970
<i>wasn't in the game, but with me?</i>

00:09:02.270 --> 00:09:04.840
<i>My guilty feelings caused me
to let my guard down.</i>

00:09:06.170 --> 00:09:08.280
<i>Crap! Akuma needs to
take control again, fast!</i>

00:09:14.120 --> 00:09:15.950
<i>Final Atomic Buster!</i>

00:09:19.690 --> 00:09:22.660
<i>She came from behind
to tie it up at one-all.</i>

00:09:23.760 --> 00:09:25.530
<i>While doggedly defending,</i>

00:09:26.260 --> 00:09:29.560
<i>she waited for my pride as a gamer
to cause me to falter...</i>

00:09:31.330 --> 00:09:33.530
<i>due to my desire to win by fighting fair</i>

00:09:34.140 --> 00:09:36.070
<i>and my desire to win
with superior technique.</i>

00:09:41.480 --> 00:09:44.650
<i>My desire to win a fight
fair and square...</i>

00:09:45.110 --> 00:09:47.210
<i>That's what she was aiming for! But...</i>

00:09:49.650 --> 00:09:51.990
<i>My Zanku Hadoken isn't working anymore!</i>

00:09:54.760 --> 00:09:56.620
<i>I tremble even when he gets close!</i>

00:09:58.730 --> 00:10:01.600
<i>A Screw Piledriver while walking?
How is that possible?</i>

00:10:03.230 --> 00:10:06.400
<i>You have to spin the lever around,
so you usually jump.</i>

00:10:11.270 --> 00:10:13.770
<i>She spins it with a flick of her fingers?</i>

00:10:15.040 --> 00:10:16.040
<i>She is...</i>

00:10:17.750 --> 00:10:19.050
<i>truly astounding!</i>

00:10:21.880 --> 00:10:24.650
<i>It only makes sense
that she would steal Yaguchi's heart.</i>

00:10:37.730 --> 00:10:39.570
<i>If Ono's strength at this is...</i>

00:10:41.400 --> 00:10:43.640
<i>as strong as her love for Yaguchi...</i>

00:10:45.410 --> 00:10:47.380
<i>then the level of my love is...</i>

00:10:51.910 --> 00:10:54.050
<i>nothing compared to hers!</i>

00:11:17.240 --> 00:11:20.210
"Recognize, decide," and what's the other?

00:11:20.740 --> 00:11:21.780
"Motion"?

00:11:21.840 --> 00:11:24.110
"Action." You almost got it right.

00:11:26.610 --> 00:11:29.720
Don't you think
the three main components of driving

00:11:30.180 --> 00:11:33.350
are just like those in the games
you love so much, Haruo?

00:11:33.850 --> 00:11:35.120
Especially in fighting games.

00:11:35.320 --> 00:11:37.590
Don't say things like that!

00:11:37.860 --> 00:11:40.130
Driving will end up like
playing a game to me!

00:11:40.330 --> 00:11:43.100
I guess you're right.
It could put people in danger.

00:11:43.530 --> 00:11:48.640
<i>Jeez! To make things worse, the arrows
on the signs look like joystick commands!</i>

00:11:48.700 --> 00:11:49.840
<i>Sonic Boom!</i>

00:11:51.370 --> 00:11:53.170
You've even started liking girls.

00:11:53.240 --> 00:11:54.780
What's that all about?

00:11:54.840 --> 00:11:56.340
I bet it's because of Ono.

00:11:56.880 --> 00:11:59.010
I can tell even though you're hiding it.

00:11:59.080 --> 00:12:02.280
You're the kind of guy who doesn't
know much about love and romance.

00:12:04.790 --> 00:12:07.290
You don't know what to do
for the girl on your mind,

00:12:07.620 --> 00:12:10.260
so you're struggling hard
to make changes in yourself.

00:12:11.330 --> 00:12:12.860
I think it's a good thing.

00:12:13.730 --> 00:12:16.700
You're unconsciously striving to
improve yourself and be a nice guy.

00:12:17.530 --> 00:12:18.500
But, you know,

00:12:19.070 --> 00:12:20.800
that's what love is, Haruo!

00:12:21.470 --> 00:12:25.240
The woman in your heart is
spurring you on toward change!

00:12:26.140 --> 00:12:27.170
Miyao,

00:12:27.240 --> 00:12:30.810
I want to ride a scooter because
it's faster and easier to get around.

00:12:31.180 --> 00:12:33.250
I also think it looks pretty cool.

00:12:33.310 --> 00:12:34.180
Oh, I see.

00:12:34.850 --> 00:12:38.420
<i>Was I reading too much into it?
I was sure I had read him right.</i>

00:12:38.490 --> 00:12:40.890
Well, Haruo.

00:12:41.360 --> 00:12:45.130
It's unusual to see you studying
during break time.

00:12:45.190 --> 00:12:47.600
Haruo wants to get a scooter license.

00:12:47.660 --> 00:12:52.030
A scooter license? I thought you were
only interested in games. How come?

00:12:52.100 --> 00:12:55.570
What does it matter? Is it that strange
for me to want a scooter license?

00:12:55.640 --> 00:12:57.070
Yes, it's strange.

00:12:58.640 --> 00:13:00.210
Listen, Haruo.

00:13:01.040 --> 00:13:04.210
A new console system is
being released soon, right?

00:13:04.610 --> 00:13:07.520
Are you sure you want to spend
your money on a license?

00:13:07.580 --> 00:13:09.950
I'm a second-year high school student!

00:13:10.380 --> 00:13:13.490
I'm not a kid who's all excited
about games all the time.

00:13:13.550 --> 00:13:14.660
Really?

00:13:18.890 --> 00:13:23.360
Say, aren't you trying to get a license
to ride a scooter?

00:13:23.430 --> 00:13:25.430
Won't you get
bad driving habits from that?

00:13:25.500 --> 00:13:27.200
I'm doing it to help me train.

00:13:27.670 --> 00:13:30.300
Don't drive like that in real life.

00:13:30.740 --> 00:13:34.240
It isn't like your ordinary game,
so don't try to pass on corners.

00:13:34.810 --> 00:13:36.680
-I can't?
-Of course not!

00:13:37.110 --> 00:13:39.810
Don't feel like you have to be number one.

00:13:39.880 --> 00:13:42.580
Number one at what? Of course I won't.

00:13:43.650 --> 00:13:47.050
But I get the feeling
I'll see a countdown clock in my head.

00:13:47.120 --> 00:13:48.390
That's dangerous.

00:13:48.860 --> 00:13:52.090
Unless you stop thinking about it
like a game, you'll end up dying.

00:13:52.160 --> 00:13:54.860
Listen!
There's no continue button in life.

00:13:55.400 --> 00:13:57.730
You don't get your life back
by feeding it 100 yen.

00:13:58.400 --> 00:14:00.170
I know!

00:14:00.230 --> 00:14:01.070
Damn!

00:14:04.000 --> 00:14:06.140
Fine. I give up.

00:14:07.010 --> 00:14:07.940
There!

00:14:10.810 --> 00:14:14.580
If I get a license and buy a scooter,
I can't buy games.

00:14:15.220 --> 00:14:17.690
I'll have to be patient for a while.

00:14:17.750 --> 00:14:19.250
Are you sure you can?

00:14:19.320 --> 00:14:22.560
I doubt you have any patience at all
when it comes to games.

00:14:22.620 --> 00:14:24.160
Damn right I do!

00:14:24.230 --> 00:14:27.530
Really? Won't your gamer's heart
keep pestering you?

00:14:28.860 --> 00:14:31.430
<i>The King of Fighters '95</i> for Saturn.

00:14:32.400 --> 00:14:34.540
<i>Mortal Kombat II Complete Edition.</i>

00:14:35.300 --> 00:14:37.400
<i>Street Fighter II: The Animated Movie.</i>

00:14:38.310 --> 00:14:41.180
There are so many appealing games.

00:14:41.980 --> 00:14:45.380
Cut it out! You're making me
lose control of my body!

00:14:45.450 --> 00:14:48.980
Damn you, Doi!
Why are you torturing me like that?

00:14:50.890 --> 00:14:52.450
Because I can't stand you.

00:14:52.520 --> 00:14:54.790
I've always thought
you were a moron, Haruo,

00:14:54.860 --> 00:14:57.990
but if you start riding a scooter,
you'll be even better than me.

00:14:59.290 --> 00:15:01.330
You sure are honest about your feelings.

00:15:01.400 --> 00:15:05.600
Look! There are some very appealing
software here too!

00:15:06.130 --> 00:15:08.600
I bought that at the shop
first thing in the morning.

00:15:08.670 --> 00:15:11.570
Really? Kage-Maru, of course,
but Jeffry too?

00:15:11.770 --> 00:15:13.040
Damn right!

00:15:14.940 --> 00:15:16.510
What's wrong with that?

00:15:33.660 --> 00:15:36.330
<i>This soundtrack is really relaxing.</i>

00:15:36.860 --> 00:15:39.130
<i>It's perfect for studying.</i>

00:15:45.110 --> 00:15:46.540
Boo!

00:15:47.310 --> 00:15:48.780
What a hard worker!

00:15:48.840 --> 00:15:51.780
It's such a beautiful sight
to see my son studying.

00:15:52.280 --> 00:15:54.680
I'm so happy, I could walk on air.

00:15:54.750 --> 00:15:55.920
Mom.

00:15:55.980 --> 00:15:58.790
I'm so impressed to see my son
improving himself.

00:15:59.620 --> 00:16:00.450
In what?

00:16:00.850 --> 00:16:04.530
I mean, you suddenly said
you want to get a scooter license.

00:16:04.590 --> 00:16:06.090
Oh, that?

00:16:06.790 --> 00:16:08.030
You know what?

00:16:08.530 --> 00:16:10.000
You should get a license.

00:16:10.060 --> 00:16:12.930
A license? Why would I need that?

00:16:13.000 --> 00:16:14.970
It's convenient having a scooter.

00:16:15.040 --> 00:16:18.770
Why not boost your status a little
instead of just your gameplay?

00:16:19.240 --> 00:16:21.480
It might turn you into more of a man.

00:16:21.540 --> 00:16:24.380
Sitting in front of a screen,
you can't feel the wind.

00:16:25.710 --> 00:16:26.750
Besides,

00:16:27.380 --> 00:16:29.920
you think of Akira as a rival, don't you?

00:16:29.980 --> 00:16:32.390
Not just in games, but in life as well.

00:16:33.190 --> 00:16:35.360
That girl can do anything she tries.

00:16:35.420 --> 00:16:38.190
She's so good at learning stuff,
it's hard to believe we're sisters.

00:16:38.660 --> 00:16:40.660
Well, I would agree with that.

00:16:40.730 --> 00:16:44.330
She'll get herself a driver's license
before you know it.

00:16:44.400 --> 00:16:45.930
How will you feel then?

00:16:46.570 --> 00:16:49.140
As a young man,
you'll feel inferior to her

00:16:49.200 --> 00:16:53.070
and think she's better than you,
then you'll end up growing farther apart.

00:16:53.470 --> 00:16:58.250
I've got it! If you get your license,
I'll give you this scooter.

00:16:58.580 --> 00:17:00.580
Ride this over to our place, all right?

00:17:01.020 --> 00:17:02.750
I'm not so sure...

00:17:02.820 --> 00:17:06.920
I can only imagine the look on her face
when she sees how you've changed.

00:17:07.820 --> 00:17:09.020
Don't you want to see that?

00:17:10.390 --> 00:17:12.290
Improve yourself, kid!

00:17:13.260 --> 00:17:14.760
<i>I see. So it was Makoto.</i>

00:17:15.800 --> 00:17:18.730
But I am a little worried, as your mother.

00:17:19.200 --> 00:17:21.700
What if you got into an accident
or got hurt?

00:17:22.200 --> 00:17:24.170
Don't you worry about that, Mom.

00:17:24.740 --> 00:17:27.070
<i>You may not think it,
but I'm built pretty sturdy.</i>

00:17:27.740 --> 00:17:32.580
By the way, Haruo, this sexy video
of this guy on your TV...

00:17:33.510 --> 00:17:34.620
What the heck is this?

00:17:53.970 --> 00:17:57.570
Oh... is this what you're into?

00:17:57.640 --> 00:17:59.010
No way!

00:19:09.140 --> 00:19:10.210
<i>Dang!</i>

00:19:10.280 --> 00:19:13.450
<i>I haven't studied this hard
since the high school entrance exams.</i>

00:19:19.620 --> 00:19:23.790
There are 50 questions on the test.
Your 30 minutes start now.

00:19:24.460 --> 00:19:25.760
<i>Let's do this!</i>

00:19:26.630 --> 00:19:29.460
<i>Just like memorizing
the complex commands for moves,</i>

00:19:29.530 --> 00:19:32.430
<i>I've hammered the traffic rules
into my head until I got sick of them!</i>

00:19:34.170 --> 00:19:36.070
<i>I won't let any trick questions
trip me up either!</i>

00:19:36.440 --> 00:19:37.910
<i>Stay calm and think.</i>

00:19:37.970 --> 00:19:41.180
<i>Remember what you studied
and think carefully.</i>

00:19:42.180 --> 00:19:43.140
<i>But, you know,</i>

00:19:43.810 --> 00:19:47.280
<i>looking back at the kid I was,
who used to think of nothing but games,</i>

00:19:47.710 --> 00:19:52.150
<i>I can hardly believe I'm actually
taking a test to get a scooter license.</i>

00:19:53.250 --> 00:19:57.190
<i>Just like the game industry,
I'm going to keep improving too!</i>

00:20:01.660 --> 00:20:03.300
<i>Yahoo!</i>

00:20:04.400 --> 00:20:07.770
<i>The streets of Mizonokuchi
look totally different now!</i>

00:20:08.270 --> 00:20:11.340
<i>I wonder how Ono will react
when she sees me like this.</i>

00:20:11.810 --> 00:20:14.510
<i>Now, I can prove that
I'm not just a gaming fool.</i>

00:20:16.610 --> 00:20:19.880
<i>You know, I think I lied to Miyao.</i>

00:20:20.380 --> 00:20:24.220
<i>I told him it was faster
and easier to get around.</i>

00:20:24.690 --> 00:20:28.320
<i>What he said just may have been right.</i>

00:20:36.960 --> 00:20:38.600
Yo! You're here, kid!

00:20:39.070 --> 00:20:41.840
I think she's around the back. Go see her.

00:20:41.900 --> 00:20:43.340
Thanks!

00:20:47.140 --> 00:20:49.280
It's so nice being young.

00:20:59.050 --> 00:21:00.820
Hello, Miss Akira.

00:21:01.620 --> 00:21:05.260
What do you think?
I wanted to show off to you first.

00:21:05.630 --> 00:21:07.330
Hard to believe, isn't it?

00:21:09.030 --> 00:21:12.130
Your sister gave me this scooter too.

00:21:14.670 --> 00:21:18.540
What? You worried if I can drive safely
since I'm such a game nerd?

00:21:19.740 --> 00:21:21.140
Don't you worry.

00:21:21.210 --> 00:21:23.440
I've given up
that dangerous way of thinking.

00:21:23.510 --> 00:21:26.450
But I do think about
the countdown clock a little.

00:21:27.510 --> 00:21:29.420
Now it's easier to get around.

00:21:29.750 --> 00:21:32.420
If you ever want to get out
for some fun, let me know.

00:21:32.890 --> 00:21:34.860
We'll ride on this and fly off!

00:21:55.040 --> 00:21:55.940
Ono?

00:23:37.810 --> 00:23:41.150
<i>I really wonder if there are feelings
that can't be expressed in words.</i>

00:23:41.380 --> 00:23:44.450
<i>If there really are things like that,
how can we communicate them?</i>

00:23:44.520 --> 00:23:46.850
<i>If words are no good,
then letters and calls are no good.</i>
